---
import LabLayout from '../../layouts/LabLayout.astro';
import NewsTicker from '../../components/NewsTicker.svelte';
import BenchLab from '../../components/BenchLab.astro';
---
<LabLayout title="The workshop" description="Experiments, live news and small browser tools from TRAVNY: benchmarks, interactive remakes and field notes worth a click.">
  <h1>The workshop</h1>
  <p class="lede">Live news, browser workbenches and experiments from the TRAVNY workshop.</p>
  <BenchLab />
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="bench-details" style="margin-top:32px">
    <h2 id="bench-details">What can I do with these tools?</h2>
    <article id="streambench">
      <h3><a href="https://streambench.bartek.lol/">Streambench: IPTV, radio and playlist workbench</a></h3>
      <p>Play and diagnose live audio, video and HLS streams. Open local M3U/M3U8 playlists, inspect stream types, import XMLTV guide data, and search or edit playlist entries.</p>
      <p>Save favorites, export playlists and browse public provider catalogs. Playback needs a reachable source and a compatible browser; availability depends on the provider.</p>
    </article>
    <article id="codebench">
      <h3><a href="https://codebench.bartek.lol/">Codebench: QR code and barcode generator and scanner</a></h3>
      <p>Create and style QR codes; generate Code 128, EAN, Data Matrix, Aztec and PDF417 codes. Scan images from local files or a supported camera, and export the result as images or vector graphics.</p>
      <p>Use it for sharing links, Wi-Fi information, labels and inventory identifiers without uploading the payload to a Codebench backend.</p>
    </article>
    <article id="docbench">
      <h3><a href="https://docbench.bartek.lol/">Docbench: local document and PDF tools</a></h3>
      <p>Inspect files, edit text and Markdown, validate and format JSON, YAML or XML, and review metadata. Open documents, merge supported text files and save changes locally.</p>
      <p>Preview and merge PDFs, reorder or delete pages, edit bookmarks, optimize PDF output and convert supported DOCX files. Document processing happens in the browser; PDF-to-DOCX conversion is structure-first, not a pixel-perfect layout replica.</p>
    </article>
    <p>See the shared <a href="/lab/privacy/">privacy and data-handling policy</a> for local inputs, network requests and optional agent access.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="grid">
    <NewsTicker client:visible />
    <section class="panel">
      <h2>Field notes</h2>
      <p>Ideas and experiments from the workshop.</p>
      <a href="/lab/field-notes/">Read the notes ↗</a>
    </section>
    <section class="panel">
      <h2>Token Worldcup</h2>
      <p>Compare languages in the report or count tokens in your own text.</p>
      <a href="/teksty/token-worldcup/">Open Token Worldcup ↗</a> · <a href="/lab/tokenizer/">Tokenizer playground ↗</a> ·
      <a href="https://token-worldcup.travny.chatgpt.site/">Interactive remake ↗</a>
    </section>
    <section class="panel">
      <h2>TRAVNY Radio</h2>
      <p>Continuous experimental Internet radio with live track titles, cover artwork and public metadata.</p>
      <a href="/radio/">About the radio ↗</a> ·
      <a href="https://radio.bartek.lol/">Listen live ↗</a>
    </section>
    <section class="panel">
      <h2>Badges</h2>
      <p>Ecosystem, bot and AI badges plus live counters and status, ready to paste as Markdown or HTML.</p>
      <a href="/badges/">Open the catalogue ↗</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</LabLayout>
